<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - July 11.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - July 11.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-07-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Thursday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10</p>
<p>Rank Name			P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	 394.06   7.96</p>
<p> 2   Kidston Gold	   212.50   1.02</p>
<p> 3   Ranger Minerals	177.88   3.70</p>
<p> 4   Syd Hrbr Casino	171.07   2.07</p>
<p> 5   Perilya Mines	  129.27   0.53</p>
<p> 6   Natl In Prop	   128.41   1.13</p>
<p> 7   Westpac Prop Tr	112.50   1.80</p>
<p> 8   Tap Oil		   83.52   1.47</p>
<p> 9   Consol Paper	    79.12   2.69</p>
<p>10   Broken Hill Pty	 72.03  18.77</p>
<p>Lowest 10</p>
<p> 1   Climax Mining	    1.67   0.83</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    3.88   0.87</p>
<p> 3   Jardine Fm China	 5.20   0.77</p>
<p> 4   Renison Goldflds	 6.00   4.09</p>
<p> 5   Haoma Mining	     6.48   0.32</p>
<p> 6   Mt Leyshon Gold	  6.88   1.60</p>
<p> 7   Croesus Min		7.00   0.35</p>
<p> 8   McPhersons		 7.05   2.45</p>
<p> 9   Gwalia Consol	    7.25   1.40</p>
<p>10   Eagle Min		  7.51   2.14</p>
<p>-- Sydney newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
</text>
